{"qid":"Q1317991","names":["Đại Việt"],"title":"Đại Việt","endonym":null,"capsule":"This entry represents the Mạc dynasty period of Đại Việt, a Vietnamese state established when Mạc Đăng Dung usurped the throne from the Lê dynasty in 1527. After the Lê restoration in 1592 drove the Mạc from Hanoi (Thăng Long), the dynasty retreated to the northern highland province of Cao Bằng, where it continued under Ming Chinese protection until the Lê-Trịnh forces finally extinguished it in 1677. The broader Đại Việt polity continued under Lê nominal kings and Trịnh lords in the north and Nguyễn lords in the south until reunification under Emperor Gia Long (Nguyễn Ánh) and the proclamation of Vietnam in 1804.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Vietnamese dynastic chronicles and Ming Chinese records document the Mạc period; territorial extent during the Cao Bằng refuge phase is limited and reasonably well defined, but the broader Đại Việt boundary for this period involves scholarly reconstruction.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Mạc dynasty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%E1%BA%A1c_dynasty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Đại Việt","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C4%90%E1%BA%A1i_Vi%E1%BB%87t"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Mạc dynasty","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Lê Thái Tổ","nativeName":"黎太祖","roman":"Lê Thái Tổ","start":1428,"end":1433,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Lê Thái Tông","nativeName":"黎太宗","roman":"Lê Thái Tông","start":1433,"end":1442,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Lê Nhân Tông","nativeName":"